m the `ak.stock_zh_a_spot_em()` call. I will move this call to a separate function, giving the user immediate access to their holdings, even with potentially outdated pricing data. I am adding a \"refresh\" button to update real-time quotes, and I'll consider incorporating a timeout. I'm exploring the `st.empty()` placeholder for asynchronous updates, but I'm constrained by Streamlit's top-down execution model. I will also increase the cache duration for `get_realtime_quotes`.\n\n\n**Implementing UI and Logic Adjustments**\n\nI'm now focusing on a plan to significantly improve the user experience. The feedback highlights that real-time market data retrieval is too slow, and can even cause the page to appear frozen. I'm exploring an approach of showing the static data first, then fetching the real-time quotes in the background, offering a \"refresh\" button to update them. Additionally, I'll provide the user with the ability to toggle real-time market data to prevent the issue of slow loading times.\n\n\n",
